[[34m2026-06-15 08:11:53[0m] use_crossview_encoder=True
[[34m2026-06-15 08:11:53[0m] fusion_mode='cross_attention'
[[34m2026-06-15 08:11:53[0m]   -> Bidirectional cross-attention between views: each view attends to the other view’s tokens, then features are combined for the rest of the encoder/decoder. Strong when views are aligned but not identical.
[[34m2026-06-15 08:11:53[0m] view_in=8, view_mixing_strategy=embedding
[[34m2026-06-15 08:11:53[0m] use_view_embedding vs use_viewwise_decoder_lora: per-view additive embeddings bias early (or latent) features with a small vector per view; viewwise_decoder_lora adds low-rank adapters on the decoder side conditioned by view index—typically more flexible than a single embedding per view for reconstruction, at the cost of more trainable parameters.
[[34m2026-06-15 08:11:53[0m]   use_view_embedding=False
[[34m2026-06-15 08:11:53[0m]   use_viewwise_decoder_lora=False
[[34m2026-06-15 08:11:53[0m] use_lora=True, use_lora_before=False, use_lora_after=True, lora_rank=32. Before = LoRA on the encoder stem / early downsampling; after = bottleneck and later decoder. Both can be enabled for two complementary adaptation regions.
